This shows an **amber warning icon** with a tooltip when the customer has a posting restriction. Passing `false` renders nothing. It uses inline SVG, so no icon library is required.

Add this helper to your `.cshtml`:

```cshtml
@helper PostingRestrictionIcon(bool hasPostingRestriction)
{
    if (hasPostingRestriction)
    {
        <span class="posting-restriction-icon"
              title="Customer has a posting restriction"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Customer has a posting restriction">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                 viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                 fill="none"
                 stroke="currentColor"
                 stroke-width="1.8"
                 stroke-linecap="round"
                 stroke-linejoin="round"
                 aria-hidden="true"
                 focusable="false">
                <path d="M12 3 2 21h20L12 3Z" />
                <path d="M12 9v5" />
                <circle cx="12" cy="17" r="1"
                        fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
            </svg>
        </span>
    }
}
```

Add this CSS to your stylesheet, or inside a `<style>` block in the page:

```css
.posting-restriction-cell {
    text-align: center;
    vertical-align: middle;
}

.posting-restriction-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border: 1px solid #f0d28a;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background-color: #fff8e6;
    color: #925900;
    vertical-align: middle;
    cursor: help;
}

.posting-restriction-icon svg {
    display: block;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
}
```

Then call it inside your table column, replacing `customer.HasPostingRestriction` with your actual property or condition:

```cshtml
<td class="posting-restriction-cell">
    @PostingRestrictionIcon(customer.HasPostingRestriction)
</td>
```

This follows the classic MVC `@helper` syntax in your example. **ASP.NET Core MVC does not support `@helper`.** ([learn.microsoft.com][1])

